Cell["The most important keys the user will need are:", "Text",
 CellID->1427,ExpressionUUID->"38c21acd-78aa-45da-a588-55913f73b401"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["Symbol"], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "14d0aa00-c0e5-4130-8e1d-559ae14c3f0a"],
 ": it serves a dual purpose \[LongDash] on one hand it is what xAct needs \
for the definition (below we have a tensor-valued form: xAct needs an actual \
symbol ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["F", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "0302dab6-518f-4fbd-95ed-51050b6b25fd"],
 " and the index of a previously defined vector bundle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[GothicCapitalI]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "20142168-abf3-4e44-9603-76289c45a1a3"],
 "); on the other hand it is how SolutionsX recognizes this object in the \
database, simply by the symbol ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["F", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "6140a4c1-8348-4688-971b-bb573579b43a"],
 ". When such a composite Symbol appears in the association, SolutionsX knows \
how to strip it automatically, through the internal function ",
 Cell[BoxData["makeKey"], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "6bfd9b9e-976c-4f03-a007-8a2036bc3c04"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1428,ExpressionUUID->"83822617-6a8d-4a49-aaf3-72620bdb9c56"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["Expression"], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "89b225d5-a61c-4e61-883f-849893fd5d15"],
 ": where the user fills in the physically relevant data. In this example the \
vector bundle is supposed to be three-dimensional, and the form is the same \
for each value of the index ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[GothicCapitalI]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "44689381-b10f-4363-82bc-fb0040187221"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1429,ExpressionUUID->"87463afa-ecdc-4cc7-ad0a-7ed4b356a4ff"],

